# Point clouds are never committed — regenerate synthetic scenes with
#   python -m avr25d.synth
# and fetch KITTI with ../tools/fetch_kitti.py
#
# `data/*` rather than `data/`: git does not descend into an excluded
# directory, so the exported models below could not be re-included otherwise.
data/*

# ...except the exported ONNX models. 4.6 MB for both, and committing them
# means a fresh clone can run the network without a 3.6 MB checkpoint
# download and a PyTorch install. See data/models/NOTICE.md for the licence.
!data/models/
data/models/*
!data/models/*.onnx
!data/models/NOTICE.md

# ...and the Day 10 fine-tuned weights, 3.6 MB each. They are committed as
# *evidence*, not as something the pipeline loads: neither beats the pretrained
# network on mIoU, config.yaml still points at the ONNX, and the point of
# keeping them is that "we tried and it did not help" is a claim someone can
# check rather than take on trust. Reproducing them costs a 4-minute train and
# a 6-minute eval, which is cheap but not free, and the result is seed-
# dependent.
!data/models/*.pt

# The split manifest and the evaluations that judged those weights. A few kB,
# and without them the .pt files are unexplained binaries: the manifest says
# which sequences trained and which validated, the reports say what the answer
# was. Same rule as the models — provenance travels with the artefact.
!data/splits/
data/splits/*
!data/splits/*.json
!data/finetune_report*.json

# The FR-40 scene registry: every scene's exact ground truth in the shape the
# `scenes` collection stores (IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN §8). 20 kB, derived from the
# committed CSVs alone — no ray-casting and no dataset — and deterministic, so
# regenerating it is a no-op diff. Tracked because the Next.js seed reads it
# from a fresh clone, and because a number the dashboard shows should be in the
# repo next to the CSV that specifies it.
!data/scenes_registry.json

# The demo fallback replay log (Path C safety net) stays OUT of git, and it is
# not a preference — it cannot go in. A frame is ~1.85 MB whatever the
# perception mode, so even a 55-frame log clears GitHub's hard 100 MB
# per-file limit and the push is rejected outright; the 271-frame log this
# was written for is 471 MB. Tracking it would also add half a gigabyte to
# every clone forever, and `git pull` on the VM is the documented redeploy
# path (docs/DEPLOYMENT.md §14).
#
# Ship it instead — the log is transferred by scp during deployment and
# regenerated locally by one command. Both are documented in
# docs/DEPLOYMENT.md §8:
#     python -m avr25d.server.app --infer geometric --seq 04 \
#         --data data/kitti --record data/logs/demo.log
data/logs/

__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
build/
dist/

# Scratch/variant benchmark outputs remain ignored, but authoritative results.json
# is tracked for the team (deck numbers hand-off C3 and MongoDB publish H2).
results_*.json

